Third-party components in stemd packages
========================================

stemd itself is under MIT or Apache-2.0, at your option: LICENSE-MIT and
LICENSE-APACHE beside this file. The models are not covered by that licence.
stemd's own model, stemd_roformer, is CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, and the other models
keep the terms their authors give them. Each model's terms sit beside its
weights as <artefact>.LICENSE.txt.

Each entry names the packages that contain it:

  all       every package
  macOS     Stemd.app
  Windows   the installer and the zip
  Linux     the deb, the rpm and the AppImage

Licence texts beside this file:

  THIRD-PARTY-CRATES        the Rust crates and the text of each crate's licence
  MLX.txt                   MLX and the libraries built into it
  InstrumentSans-OFL.txt    SIL Open Font License 1.1
  LGPL-2.0.txt              GNU Library General Public License version 2
  GPL-3.0.txt               GNU General Public License version 3, which the
                            LGPL-3.0 text in THIRD-PARTY-CRATES supplements
  Sparkle.txt               Sparkle
  LICENSE-APACHE            Apache License 2.0

Rust crates (all), compiled into stemd-server and stemd-cli
  Listed by licence, with each licence text, in THIRD-PARTY-CRATES.
  scripts/crate-notices.sh generates that file with cargo-about.

MLX 0.32.4 (all), compiled into stemd-server
  Copyright 2023 Apple Inc. MIT. MLX builds in mlx-c, fmt, nlohmann/json and
  gguf-tools (MIT) on every platform; metal-cpp (Apache-2.0) on macOS; NVIDIA
  cudnn-frontend (MIT), NVTX (Apache-2.0 with LLVM exceptions) and CUTLASS
  (BSD-3-Clause) on Windows and Linux; and dlfcn-win32 (MIT) on Windows. The
  texts are in MLX.txt.

Instrument Sans (all), compiled into stemd-server
  Copyright 2022 The Instrument Sans Project Authors. SIL Open Font License
  1.1, text in InstrumentSans-OFL.txt.

LAME 3.100 (all), statically linked into stemd-server
  LGPL-2.0 (GNU Library General Public License version 2), text in
  LGPL-2.0.txt. Source: https://lame.sourceforge.io/
  The Rust bindings, mp3lame-sys and mp3lame-encoder, are LGPL-3.0; see
  THIRD-PARTY-CRATES. The source of stemd is at https://github.com/nsaintot/stemd,
  and docs/building.md there shows how to rebuild stemd-server, so it can be
  relinked against a modified LAME.

Sparkle 2.10.0 (macOS), Contents/Frameworks/Sparkle.framework
  MIT, with the notices of the code it includes. Text in Sparkle.txt.

